## 3. COMPLETE API ROUTE CLASSIFICATION & INVENTORY

Every single route in `backend/app/api/` has been classified based on whether it connects to live external systems, queries the local relational database, operates via simulation adapters, or executes algorithmic rules.

### 3.1 Meteorological & Environmental Intelligence (`weather.py`)
| Endpoint | Method | Classification | Mechanism & Reality |
|---|---|---|---|
| `/api/v1/weather` | GET | **LIVE EXTERNAL** | Queries `api.open-meteo.com/v1/forecast` with 15-min in-memory cache. |
| `/api/v1/weather/search` | GET | **LIVE EXTERNAL** | Queries `geocoding-api.open-meteo.com/v1/search` in real time. |
| `/api/v1/weather/locations` | GET | **STATIC CATALOG** | Returns coordinate registry of 14 NER transportation hubs. |
| `/api/v1/weather/current` | GET | **LIVE EXTERNAL** | Live Open-Meteo current condition payload. |
| `/api/v1/weather/forecast` | GET | **LIVE EXTERNAL** | Live 7-day temperature, rainfall, and wind forecast. |
| `/api/v1/weather/route-risk` | POST | **LIVE COMPUTATION** | Fetches live weather for corridor waypoints & calculates slip risk. |
| `/api/v1/weather/{city_name}` | GET | **LIVE EXTERNAL** | Dynamic coordinate resolution and live weather fetch. |

